From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Electron contributors <electron@github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: fix: route injected mouse input through frame capture

Expose event-aware target resolution and validated mouse dispatch so injected
input retains native cross-frame enter/leave notifications and capture checks.
A trusted target hint supports frames without a current visible surface, while
pointer lock, active capture and DevTools routing keep their native precedence.

Keep callback requests separate from coalescible native events and complete
abandoned event callbacks asynchronously. Revalidate view registration and the
ancestor chain before returning targets and before dispatching injected input.

Preserve injected chorded-button capture until the final button is released,
without changing native platform MouseUp handling.

